# Public SSH keys allowed to sign a release tag.
# This is the public copy shipped in the tree. The runtime trust anchor is the
# host copy outside the checkout (~/.config/digithings/allowed_signers, or
# --allowed-signers); ssh_signers.py refuses a signers file that lives inside
# the repository it verifies.
#
# One key per line, sshd allowed-signers format:
#   <email> [options] <key-type> <public-key> [comment]
#
# The release key is the agent-held software Ed25519 primary (D-S1, 2026-11-09).
# The 2026-12-01 bound keeps the tags cut before it verifiable; K2 adds the
# rotating 2027-06-01 line. New tags use the current agent key; no hardware
# token is involved.
# A file with no key lines fails closed: every deploy job refuses the tag.
# Do not put a private key in this file.
release@digithings namespaces="git",valid-before="20261201Z" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIKVY/JXX9piwuPgbYu7hx7CsprAMaOcSlxGoK4oVBmbp K1 2026-11-09
# K2: rotating agent key; the 2026 line above remains until its bound.
release@digithings namespaces="git",valid-before="20270601Z" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIBLmqNgbV0gtFcG1Lw0Bg8iYQSCiM49XR3wrFa6Gkn7x K2 2026-11-09
